# How the app gets its pages. `remote`: a static SPA that signs in at the issuer below. `local`: the whole app with its
# own server and sqlite database, bundled as a sidecar (needs Bun to build). Run `pnpm desktop:init --force` after
# switching, so src-tauri/ matches the mode.
DESKTOP_MODE=remote

# --- Remote mode ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The OAuth server (issuer) the app signs in at, and the API it calls with the access token. Baked into the build.
# A Frigear server on this machine (the standalone mobile starter's apps/web, say): http://localhost:3000.
# frigear.nu or your own issuer: its https origin, and register the redirect URIs from identity.ts there.
NUXT_PUBLIC_AUTHENTICATION_CLIENT_ISSUER=http://localhost:3000
NUXT_PUBLIC_AUTHENTICATION_CLIENT_API_BASE=http://localhost:3000

# Overrides of identity.ts, for example per environment. Leave them commented out to use identity.ts.
# Add offline_access for issuers that only issue a refresh token for it (Keycloak, Auth0, ...).
# NUXT_PUBLIC_AUTHENTICATION_CLIENT_CLIENT_ID=desktop
# NUXT_PUBLIC_AUTHENTICATION_CLIENT_SCOPE=openid profile email offline_access

# --- Local mode ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Seals the session cookie under `pnpm dev`. `pnpm prepare:env` fills in a random one. The built app generates its own
# secrets on first start, in the user's app-data folder, so nothing here ships with it.
NUXT_APP_SECRET=
